Search file contents by regex or literal text; returns matching lines grouped by file, most recently modified files first; respects .gitignore. It shows the first {{ .MaxResults }} lines or entries, or head_limit of them, from offset: when it leaves some out it says so, and a larger offset shows the next ones. path is a file or a directory. To find files by name, use the glob tool; include (or glob) and type choose which files are searched. Set ignore_case (or -i) to match regardless of case. -A, -B and -C show lines after, before and around each match; output_mode files_with_matches lists only the files, and count how many lines match in each. The pattern is a regular expression unless literal_text is true, so escape ( ) [ ] { } . * + ? | ^ $ to match them as written: `func \(s \*Server\)` finds `func (s *Server)`. multiline lets a pattern span lines.
